  s += `Source: \`card-data-export/cards.json\` (70 verbatim seed records, identical to production for level/HP/ATK/DEF/text — see \`card-data-export/EXPORT_REPORT.md\`) and the engine in \`src/engine/\`. Branch \`docs/card-balance-review\`.\n\n`;
  s += `## 1. Summary\n\n- Cards reviewed: **${outs.length}/70** (48 characters: 39 Lv15 + 7 Lv40 + 2 Lv70; 2 support; 10 spells; 10 traps).\n- Proposed changes: **${changed.length}** cards (${outs.filter(o => o.changeType === 'def').length} DEF only, ${outs.filter(o => o.changeType === 'effect').length} effect only, ${outs.filter(o => o.changeType === 'def+effect').length} DEF + effect). Everything else is explicitly "unchanged". **HP/ATK: 0 changes.**\n- Tier counts (relative to the level mean): current ${tierCount('tierCur')}  ->  proposed ${tierCount('tierProp')}.\n- Engine proposals that are NOT data changes (new engine work): ENGINE-PROP-01..05, see \`ENGINE_COMPATIBILITY.md\` and \`CARD_CHANGELOG.md\`.\n- Honest limit: HP/ATK are locked, so the S-tier Lv15 cards (MON-015, PIKACHU-015, DNMAN-015, LINLADA-015, MELON-015, SMILE-015, CUTIE-015) stay S after the effect trims. Their power comes from the stat line. Only the owner can decide to change it.\n- No playtest data exists (production \`pvp_matches\` was empty): every tier is a **model estimate**, not a measured win rate.\n\n`;
  s += `## 2. Rubric and how progression is evaluated\n\nPower of one character = \`effective HP x effective ATK x (1 + effect bonus)\` (script: \`scripts/card-balance-model.ts\`). Tier = ratio to the mean of the same level: S >= 1.25, A >= 1.10, B >= 0.90, C >= 0.75, D < 0.75.\n\n| Assumption | Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Average incoming ATK by level | ${Object.entries(INCOMING_ATK).map(([l, a]) => `Lv${l}: ${a}`).join(', ')} | DEF converts to effective HP as HP x A/(A-DEF) |\n| Extra card | +${DRAW_VALUE * 100}% | one draw = about one unit of tempo |\n| Loot (discard 1 draw 1) | +${LOOT_VALUE * 100}% | selection only |\n| Draw-on-kill probability | ${KILL_DRAW_PROB} | |\n| "Target HP lower than self" true | ${COND_HPLOWER_PROB} | |\n| Horizon | ${HORIZON_TURNS} turns | repeated per-turn effects |\n| Attack bonus | half of the bonus counts as effective ATK | the bonus applies only when attacking |\n\nChecked per card: redundancy (identical effect on another card of the same level), power, survivability, card advantage, removal, healing, control, combos, element/class synergy, counterplay. Spells/traps are judged on source behaviour, not on the model.\n\n**Progression Lv15 -> Lv40 -> Lv70.** Means: Lv15 AP ${meanAp[15].toFixed(0)}, Lv40 ${meanAp[40].toFixed(0)}, Lv70 ${meanAp[70].toFixed(0)}. A form must cost 1 Evolution card plus 1 sacrifice (Lv40) or 2 (Lv70) face-up characters, so a Lv40 form should be clearly stronger than a Lv15 of the same chain, not merely equal. Chains below that bar (relative tier at Lv40 D): FOLLOW-YOU-040, TEE-040, LALAPING-040. Chains above (S): BADGUY-040, 1GOKU-040. The Lv70 sample has only 2 cards, so no relative balance is possible.\n\n**Evolution/Fusion** are reviewed in the EVO-001 and FUS-001 entries and in \`ENGINE_COMPATIBILITY.md\` (discrepancy with the Issue text: Evolution needs 1 Evolution card plus 1/2/3 sacrifices, not 1/2/3 Evolution cards).\n\n`;
  s += `## 3. Redundancy groups (same level, identical ability wording)\n\n`;
  const seen = new Set<string>();
